n Idaho parks, including record number at Minidoka historic site • Idaho Capital Sun","source":"https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/05/26/430000-visits-recorded-at-southern-idaho-parks-including-record-number-at-minidoka-historic-site/?utm_source=newsletters.idahocapitalsun.com&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_campaign=isp-transports-more-immigrants-to-ice-record-visitation-at-minidoka-column-rebuilding-civics-participation&_bhlid=319c5e236ce7ce3ab534787f86e8e76e75bd4231","author":["[[Christina Lords]]"],"published":"2026-05-26","created":"2026-07-08","description":"Four southern Idaho recreation sites welcomed visitors for more than 430,000 visits in 2025, including a record number of visits to the Minidoka National Historic Site near Jerome. Craters of the Moon National Monument and Preserve, Hagerman Fossil Beds National Monument, City of Rocks National Reserve, and Minidoka National Historic Site welcomed a combined 431,522 […]"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},